                <pb facs="0906" n="818" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg818"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-01-19"><hi rendition="#italic">January 19,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(In view of Mr. Leishman’s telegram of the 17th instant, Mr. Hay informs him that
                    the continued presence of the American vessels in Turkish waters seems to
                    obstruct the negotiations for the settlement of the pending question, and they
                    will therefore be withdrawn at the end of the month. Instructs him to intimate
                    that the temporary withdrawal of the vessels is directed in order to facilitate
                    prompt disposition of the pending questions.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
